## Harden the per-user XDG_RUNTIME_DIR (/run/user/%i) with noexec.
##
## systemd-logind mounts this tmpfs nosuid,nodev but NEVER noexec, and exposes no
## option to change it (the flags are hardcoded in logind), so /run/user/%i
## bypasses the noexec that remount-secure applies to /run -- it is a separate
## mount and does not inherit the parent's options.
##
## ExecStartPost runs AFTER systemd-user-runtime-dir has created, mounted and
## chowned the directory, so this never races logind and never trips logind's
## "already a mount point" skip. remount-secure --runtime-dir adds noexec only at
## level >= 2 (matching /run) and honors the 'noremountsecure' off-switch.
##
## '-' prefix: best-effort. A remount failure must NOT block login (fail open).
##
## https://www.kicksecure.com/wiki/Dev/remount-secure
[Service]
ExecStartPost=-/usr/bin/remount-secure --runtime-dir %i
